# Cipher: the card stays encoded on its creature even if the creature changes controller (CR 702.99c), and the creature's
# ability is the creature's, so its new controller controls it (the ruling: "that player will create a copy of the encoded
# card and may cast it"). Bot1 encodes Trait Doctoring on Haywire Mite. Bot2's kicked Thieving Skydiver takes the Mite
# (an artifact creature of mana value 1). When the Mite deals combat damage to Bot1 on Bot2's turn, it is Bot2 who is asked,
# who chooses the copy's target and its words, and the card, which Bot1 owns, stays in exile.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Haywire Mite
Island
Trait Doctoring
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Island
Island
Thieving Skydiver
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Haywire Mite.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Trait Doctoring.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Island)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Replace a color word)
Bot1.Colors(Blue)
Bot1.Colors(Red)
Bot1.Choose(Haywire Mite)
? Exile = Trait Doctoring
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Island#3.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Thieving Skydiver.Cast(Kicked: 1)
[T6 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot2.Battlefield = Island; Island; Island; Haywire Mite; Thieving Skydiver
[T8 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Haywire Mite)
[T8 Bot2.CombatDamage]
Bot2.Accept
Bot2.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Island)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Modes(Replace a basic land type)
Bot2.Modes(Island)
Bot2.Modes(Swamp)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Subtypes = Swamp
! Bot1.Accept

[Expect]
Turn = 8
Bot1.Life = 19
Exile = Trait Doctoring
Bot1.Graveyard =
